# --- BetterNCM-v3 checkout hygiene ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Runtime output, evidence captured from a live client, and machine-local state.  None of it is
# source, and two of these entries are a redistribution problem rather than just noise:
#
#   * out/orpheus/     the client's front-end extracted from web.pack -- NetEase copyrighted
#                      material, ~100 MB.  Rebuild it locally with tools/ntpk.py.
#   * out/repacked.ntpk  a repacked orpheus container, 36 MB.  Never ship this.
#   * out/host.json    carries the live backend's 32-character API key.
#   * out/agent.log    live agent log (paths, ports, plugin telemetry).
#   * out/host.stdout.log  the backend's own stdout: it prints `port=… key=…` when it starts, so
#                          the runtime API key lands in this file too.
#
# The small evidence files kept in out/ (perf-*.json, acceptance-*.json, verify-*.png) are
# reproducible measurements, not client assets, so they stay tracked.

/out/orpheus/
/out/libcef-try/
/out/release/
/out/repacked.ntpk
/out/agent.log
/out/agent.lock
/out/host.json
/out/host.stdout.log
/out/host.stdout.log.err
/out/bncm-data/
/out/hijack-candidates.json
/out/loader/obj/
/out/loader/*.exp
/out/loader/*.lib
/out/loader/install-manifest.json

# out/loader/version.dll IS tracked on purpose: it is a build product of loader/version_proxy,
# but tools/release/build_release.ps1 requires it to assemble both packages, and building it
# needs the MSVC toolchain (loader/build.cmd).

# --- upstream reference clones -----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Each directory under upstream/ is an independent clone with its own .git and its own upstream
# remote.  They are reference material, not part of this project; upstream/README.md records the
# exact URLs and commits to fetch.
/upstream/*
!/upstream/README.md

# --- tooling / OS noise ------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.tmp
*.bak
